    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, the full suite (the acceptance suite is the project's test set) passes with 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes:\n\n**Schema / model**\n- Added a `deleted` column to the `owners` table in all four dialect schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`), defaulting to false so existing seed rows are not-deleted. The test profile uses `hsqldb` (`ddl-auto=none`, schema-driven).\n- Added a `Boolean deleted` field (default `FALSE`) with getter/setter to `Owner.java`, mapped via `@Column(name = \"deleted\")`. A newly built owner keeps the field default (`false`) since the request DTO has no such field.\n\n**API contract**\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` response schema in `openapi.yml`. The generated `OwnerDto` gets it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so `GET` responses now carry `$.deleted`.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `DeleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner instead of hard-deleting it \u2014 the row is retained and `DELETE` still returns 204. `LoadOwner`/`GET` therefore still return the owner afterward, with `deleted: true`.\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (the identity/duplicate block) and `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (the soft-duplicate flag) now filter out owners flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Tests**: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (create \u2192 `deleted:false`, delete \u2192 GET still 200 with `deleted:true`) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreate after soft-delete succeeds) both pass.",
